Q1. $unwind — Display each product in every order as a separate document.
db.orders.aggregate([
  {
    $unwind: "$products"
  }
])

Meaning: Converts each product array element into its own output document.
Q2. $sum — Calculate total revenue generated from each product category.
db.orders.aggregate([
  {
    $unwind: "$products"
  },
  {
    $group: {
      _id: "$products.category",
      totalRevenue: {
        $sum: {
          $multiply: [
            "$products.price",
            "$products.quantity"
          ]
        }
      }
    }
  }
])

Logic: Revenue = product price × quantity, summed for each category.
Q3. $avg — Find the average order value for each city.
db.orders.aggregate([
  {
    $group: {
      _id: "$city",
      averageOrder: {
        $avg: "$totalAmount"
      }
    }
  }
])

Q4. $max — Find the most expensive product sold in each category.
db.orders.aggregate([
  {
    $unwind: "$products"
  },
  {
    $group: {
      _id: "$products.category",
      highestPrice: {
        $max: "$products.price"
      }
    }
  }
])

Q5. $min — Find the cheapest product in each category.
db.orders.aggregate([
  {
    $unwind: "$products"
  },
  {
    $group: {
      _id: "$products.category",
      lowestPrice: {
        $min: "$products.price"
      }
    }
  }
])

Q6. $ifNull — Display the customer name and coupon discount. Display 0 if the coupon is null or missing.
db.orders.aggregate([
  {
    $project: {
      _id: 0,
      customerName: 1,
      couponDiscount: {
        $ifNull: [
          "$couponDiscount",
          0
        ]
      }
    }
  }
])

Meaning: Replaces a null or missing coupon value with 0.
Q7. $filter — Display only products costing more than ₹20,000 in each order.
db.orders.aggregate([
  {
    $project: {
      customerName: 1,
      expensiveProducts: {
        $filter: {
          input: "$products",
          as: "item",
          cond: {
            $gt: [
              "$$item.price",
              20000
            ]
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
])

Meaning:
- input specifies the array.
- as gives each array element a temporary name.
- cond specifies the filtering condition.
- $$item.price accesses the current product's price.
Q8. $filter — Display only Electronics products purchased in each order.
db.orders.aggregate([
  {
    $project: {
      customerName: 1,
      electronics: {
        $filter: {
          input: "$products",
          as: "item",
          cond: {
            $eq: [
              "$$item.category",
              "Electronics"
            ]
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
])

Q9. $unwind, $group, $sum — Find the total quantity sold for each product.
db.orders.aggregate([
  {
    $unwind: "$products"
  },
  {
    $group: {
      _id: "$products.productName",
      quantitySold: {
        $sum: "$products.quantity"
      }
    }
  }
])

Meaning: Groups identical product names and adds their quantities.
Q10. $group, $push, $$ROOT — Group orders by city and display complete order details.
db.orders.aggregate([
  {
    $group: {
      _id: "$city",
      orders: {
        $push: "$$ROOT"
      }
    }
  }
])

Meaning: Creates one output document per city, with an array containing the complete order documents from that city.
